From 2d654689a29321a6221a920f9934cc52bad533cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dallas Delaney <dadelan@microsoft.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 00:45:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] erofs: retain verified dm-verity devices

Keep a bounded, opt-in LRU of zero-open dm-verity mappings so sequential signed EROFS mounts reuse verified kernel state instead of rebuilding loops and mapper tables. Scope mapper names and lifecycle locks per snapshotter root, verify the signed table before every reuse, and invalidate mappings when snapshots are removed. The regular overlayfs path remains untouched.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>

Copilot-Session: 925784b1-44a7-4d56-b04f-e527d2e0879f
